This script calculates the cosine similarity between each prompt 
and its corresponding answer. Cosine similarity is a common measure 
for comparing text similarity in natural language processing.
The script uses the pandas, sklearn.feature_extraction.text, and sklearn.metrics.pairwise libraries. 
It loads data from six JSON files, which was filtered by Likhith, concatenates them into one DataFrame, 
and calculates the cosine similarity between the prompts and answers using the TfidfVectorizer class. 
The script then adds the cosine similarity scores to the DataFrame and performs some basic statistical analysis, 
calculating the correlation between prompt length and similarity score. 
The script will be updated to analyze the correlation between prompt phrasing and similarity score.
